ause they are seeking global  recognition  they want to claim this attack whereas  it wasn't really them that performed it  but nobody really knows  who is behind them it is true that boko  haram is claiming responsibility  president buhari meantime repeatedly  promising to tackle islamist terrorism  what's gone wrong  i wish i could answer that question what  has gone wrong  he promised nigeria that he was going to  fix islamic  islamic terrorism since 2015  this is year five and we are yet to see  any improvement  in fact things have been getting worse  progressively  just about three weeks ago there was an  attack where hundred farmers were killed  by boko haram in the southeast of  nigeria  now this attack in the southwest and  this would be the very first of its kind  in southwest nigeria i mean in this  magnitude  we have hundreds of people being  kidnapped and it's even in the  in the home state of president buhari  himself he's from kastina state  so i think this is a big blow and a  message to nigerians  that the words of president buhari don't  really match the news don't really match  what we are seeing on the ground  if incidents like this keep happening  over and over again  and yet the president is coming out to  tell people that boko haram has been  technically defeated  or has been uh has been ended but we are  still seeing attacks and what is really  happening  so i think this is a question for  president buhari and his team to answer  flores tokura in lagos nigeria thank you
 

